meta {
  name: Accept invitation
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/invitations/accept
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{teammateToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "token": "{{invitationToken}}"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  Paste the token from the application log into the invitationToken environment variable first.

  Runs as the teammate (Auth/Register teammate and Login teammate), the account at inviteEmail -
  the person the invitation was for. Accepting as the invited address also flips emailVerified to
  true, because following a link sent to an address proves control of it.

  Once accepted, the teammate is in the workspace: Assignees, Comments and Projects can point at
  them through memberUserId, and Notifications/Teammate mentions you can reach your issues.

  A token works exactly once: the second attempt is 409 INVITATION_NOT_USABLE.
}
